- Updates of data relating to GHG emissions and absorptions for the years 1994 and 2000, using the 2006 IPCC guidelines;
- GHG inventory data published, disseminated and archived.

- Improved information on adaptation to climate change;
- The capacities of sectoral experts to evaluate adaptation measures and their implementation, to report on progress in the implementation of adaptation measures, are strengthened;
- Integration and strengthening of adaptation to climate change in the current institutional and political framework, in development planning processes at sectoral level
- Development of a portfolio of climate change adaptation measures adapted and gender-sensitive for priority sectors (agriculture, forestry, health, water, coastal zones.)
- Cost-benefit analysis of adaptation measures and identification of investment needs.
- Dissemination of adaptation measures and archiving of reports, documents and data produced

